+Feature: TodoMVC application
+  As a user managing tasks
+  I want a single-page todo application
+  So that I can track, organize, and complete my work
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  # --- Empty state ---
+
+  Rule: Empty state hides main and footer
+
+    Scenario: No todos are present on first load
+      Then the main section is hidden
+      And the footer section is hidden
+
+  # --- New todo creation ---
+
+  Rule: New todos are created via the input
+
+    Scenario: Creating a todo appends it to the list and clears the input
+      When I type "Buy milk" in the new-todo input and press Enter
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the first todo has title "Buy milk"
+      And the new-todo input is empty
+
+    Scenario: Whitespace-only input is rejected
+      When I type "   " in the new-todo input and press Enter
+      Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+    Scenario: Leading and trailing whitespace is trimmed from new todos
+      When I type "  Buy milk  " in the new-todo input and press Enter
+      Then the first todo has title "Buy milk"
+
+  # --- Toggle all ---
+
+  Rule: Toggle-all sets every todo's completed state
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all checks all todos when all are incomplete
+      Given I have created todos "A", "B", and "C"
+      When I click the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then all todos are completed
+      And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all unchecks all todos when all are completed
+      Given I have created and completed todos "A", "B", and "C"
+      When I click the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then no todos are completed
+      And the toggle-all checkbox is unchecked
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all reflects state when items are individually toggled
+      Given I have created todos "A" and "B"
+      When I toggle the first todo's checkbox
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is unchecked
+      When I toggle the second todo's checkbox
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  # --- Individual item ---
+
+  Rule: Individual todos can be completed and removed
+
+    Scenario: Checking a todo marks it completed
+      Given I have created todos "A" and "B"
+      When I toggle the first todo's checkbox
+      Then the first todo is completed
+      And the second todo is not completed
+
+    Scenario: Clicking destroy removes a todo
+      Given I have created todos "A" and "B"
+      When I click the destroy button on the first todo
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the first todo has title "B"
+
+  # --- Editing ---
+
+  Rule: Double-clicking a todo label activates editing mode
+
+    Scenario: Double-clicking enters edit mode with the current title
+      Given I have created a todo "Buy milk"
+      When I double-click the first todo's label
+      Then the first todo has the editing class
+      And the first todo's edit input has value "Buy milk"
+
+    Scenario: Pressing Enter while editing saves the new title
+      Given I have created a todo "Buy milk"
+      When I double-click the first todo's label
+      And I clear and type "Buy eggs" in the first todo's edit input and press Enter
+      Then the first todo has title "Buy eggs"
+      And the first todo does not have the editing class
+
+    Scenario: Pressing Escape while editing discards changes
+      Given I have created a todo "Buy milk"
+      When I double-click the first todo's label
+      And I clear and type "Buy eggs" in the first todo's edit input and press Escape
+      Then the first todo has title "Buy milk"
+      And the first todo does not have the editing class
+
+    Scenario: Saving an empty title destroys the todo
+      Given I have created a todo "Buy milk"
+      When I double-click the first todo's label
+      And I clear the first todo's edit input and press Enter
+      Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+    Scenario: Blurring the edit input saves the new title
+      Given I have created a todo "Buy milk"
+      When I double-click the first todo's label
+      And I clear and type "Buy eggs" in the first todo's edit input and blur
+      Then the first todo has title "Buy eggs"
+
+    Scenario: Blurring with empty title destroys the todo
+      Given I have created a todo "Buy milk"
+      When I double-click the first todo's label
+      And I clear the first todo's edit input and blur
+      Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  # --- Counter ---
+
+  Rule: The counter shows active todo count
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows zero items when no todos exist
+      Then the counter shows "0 items left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows correct count of active todos
+      Given I have created todos "A", "B", and "C"
+      When I toggle the first todo's checkbox
+      Then the counter shows "2 items left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter uses singular for one active todo
+      Given I have created a todo "A"
+      When I toggle the first todo's checkbox
+      Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter updates after a todo is removed
+      Given I have created todos "A" and "B"
+      When I click the destroy button on the first todo
+      Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  # --- Clear completed ---
+
+  Rule: Clear-completed removes finished todos
+
+    Scenario: Clear-completed removes all completed todos
+      Given I have created todos "A", "B", and "C"
+      When I toggle the first todo's checkbox
+      And I toggle the second todo's checkbox
+      And I click the clear-completed button
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the first todo has title "C"
+
+    Scenario: Clear-completed button is hidden when no todos are completed
+      Given I have created a todo "A"
+      Then the clear-completed button is hidden
+
+    Scenario: Clear-completed button is visible when at least one todo is completed
+      Given I have created a todo "A"
+      When I toggle the first todo's checkbox
+      Then the clear-completed button is visible
+
+  # --- Persistence ---
+
+  Rule: Todos persist across page reloads
+
+    Scenario: Todos survive a page reload
+      Given I have created todos "Buy milk" and "Walk the dog"
+      When the app is reloaded
+      Then the todo list contains 2 items
+      And the first todo has title "Buy milk"
+      And the second todo has title "Walk the dog"
+
+    Scenario: Completed state persists across page reloads
+      Given I have created todos "A" and "B"
+      When I toggle the first todo's checkbox
+      And the app is reloaded
+      Then the first todo is completed
+      And the second todo is not completed
+
+    Scenario: Todos are stored in localStorage under todos-vanillajs
+      Given I have created a todo "Test persistence"
+      Then localStorage contains key "todos-vanillajs"
+
+  # --- Routing ---
+
+  Rule: The active filter is controlled by the URL hash
+
+    Scenario: All todos are shown on the default route
+      Given I have created todos "A" and "B"
+      And I have completed the todo "A"
+      When I navigate to "#/"
+      Then the todo list contains 2 items
+
+    Scenario: Only active todos are shown on #/active
+      Given I have created todos "A" and "B"
+      And I have completed the todo "A"
+      When I navigate to "#/active"
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the first todo has title "B"
+
+    Scenario: Only completed todos are shown on #/completed
+      Given I have created todos "A" and "B"
+      And I have completed the todo "A"
+      When I navigate to "#/completed"
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the first todo has title "A"
+
+    Scenario: The active filter link is highlighted
+      Given I have created a todo "A"
+      When I navigate to "#/active"
+      Then the "Active" filter link is selected
+      When I navigate to "#/completed"
+      Then the "Completed" filter link is selected
+      When I navigate to "#/"
+      Then the "All" filter link is selected
+
+    Scenario: Completing a todo in active filter hides it
+      Given I have created todos "A" and "B"
+      When I navigate to "#/active"
+      And I toggle the first todo's checkbox
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+
+  # --- Initial focus ---
+
+  Rule: The new-todo input is focused on load
+
+    Scenario: The new-todo input receives focus when the app loads
+      Then the new-todo input is focused
